#: includes/controllers/v1/class-rest-reports-controller.php:140
msgid "Top-selling products"
msgstr "Top-selling products"

#: includes/controllers/v1/class-rest-reports-controller.php:141
msgid ""
"Products ranked by quantity sold. Revenue is NET — order-level refunds are "
"distributed proportionally across each order's line items so a refunded "
"order does not inflate product totals. Only paid statuses are included by "
"default (override via `status`). Pass `gallery` to scope the report to one "
"or more galleries."
msgstr "Products ranked by quantity sold. Revenue is NET — order-level refunds are distributed proportionally across each order's line items so a refunded order does not inflate product totals. Only paid statuses are included by default (override via `status`). Pass `gallery` to scope the report to one or more galleries."

#: includes/controllers/v1/class-rest-reports-controller.php:154
msgid "Top-selling galleries"
msgstr "Top-selling galleries"

#: includes/controllers/v1/class-rest-reports-controller.php:155
msgid ""
"Galleries ranked by net revenue. Order-level refunds are distributed "
"proportionally across each order's line items so a refunded gallery order "
"does not inflate the total. Only paid statuses are included by default "
"(override via `status`). Pass `gallery` to scope the report to a specific "
"gallery — the response then contains one row per gallery in the input, so "
"\"how much did gallery X make me?\" is a one-call answer."
msgstr "Galleries ranked by net revenue. Order-level refunds are distributed proportionally across each order's line items so a refunded gallery order does not inflate the total. Only paid statuses are included by default (override via `status`). Pass `gallery` to scope the report to a specific gallery — the response then contains one row per gallery in the input, so \"how much did gallery X make me?\" is a one-call answer."

